The audit caught a real failure the oracle loop did not: at \(N=64\), degree-greedy solved 4/8 seeds and randomized greedy solved 8/8. I will not ship that false-positive rung. I’m replacing it with a tiny explicitly demonstrative rung that the oracles must clear, and moving the first shippable rung to \(N=144\), where all three attacks are 0/8. This adjustment is driven by G6, and the rejected 64-vertex result will be documented.
